Scenario 1: Pretrained Model Predicts Only One Class in Object Detection

Project: Helmet Detection using YOLOv5

Problem: Despite having multiple classes in the dataset, the model predicts only "helmet" for every object.

Cause: Incorrect annotations, missing labels, wrong class count configuration, or dataset imbalance.

Solution:

Verify dataset annotations.
Check label files for all classes.
Ensure correct number of classes in YOLO configuration.
Balance the dataset across all classes.

==============

Scenario 2: Transfer Learning Model Trains Too Slowly on Small Dataset

Project: Face Mask Classification using ResNet50

Problem: Training takes too long and does not converge well on a small dataset (500 images).

Cause: Fine-tuning the entire pretrained model on a small dataset.

Solution:

Freeze early layers.
Train only the final classification layers.
Use ResNet50 as a feature extractor.
Reduce trainable parameters.


============

Scenario 3: Transfer Learning Works on Training Data but Fails on New Environment

Project: Tiger Detection using YOLOv8

Problem: Model performs well on daytime images but fails on night-time CCTV footage.

Cause: Domain shift between training data and deployment environment.

Solution:

Collect night-time images.
Fine-tune the model using night-time data.
Apply brightness and contrast augmentation.
Train with diverse lighting conditions.

